 &lt;div class="fig-card"&gt;&lt;img src="hero.png" alt="A Clean Room Is Not a Home. On the left, an empty glass box with a desk and a checklist. On the right, an agent works in its own lit room in a building, with keys locked in a vault below and every connection to the outside passing through a guarded gate." loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;A Clean Room Is Not a Home. On the left, an empty glass box with a desk and a checklist. On the right, an agent works in its own lit room in a building, with keys locked in a vault below and every connection to the outside passing through a guarded gate.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When I hear &amp;ldquo;sandbox&amp;rdquo; today, the picture is usually a coding agent: a container, a repo, run the tests, throw it away. That works. But an agent that answers email or runs a workflow for months is not a coding agent with a longer timeout. It lives somewhere.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>